WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.460
Every soul is a pledge for its own deeds.

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.110
So says the Qur'an.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.590
In Islam, each person
answers for what they do.

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.100
Yet Muslims also believe that
God knows and wills all things.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.880
This is al-Qadr, God's decree.

6
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.800
So if God decrees everything,
how can Muslims be free,

7
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.650
responsible and guided by conscience?

8
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.440
In this mission, you'll place Muslim
views on a line from God decides all,

9
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.290
to humans decide.

10
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.080
Then you'll meet the
Qur'an's accusing soul,

11
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.660
and ask how far an inner
voice can guide a Muslim.

12
00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:39.820
Your mission: explain how Muslims
hold together God's decree,

13
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.950
human freedom and conscience.
